## 2. Helios-n / H9 (cite; defer RTL)

From Helios arXiv:2406.08491 § resource efficiency:

- Helios-n = *n* virtual sub-graphs time-multiplexed onto one physical lattice.
- PE state in **LUTRAM** (not BRAM); context switch ≈ **1 cycle**.
- Cross-partition adjacent virtual PEs map to the **same** physical PE (avoid extra lattice edges). Heer et al. multi-context PEs are the prior art Helios adapts.
- Used when LUTs bind (e.g. d=27 Helios-4 … Helios-27; d=51 Helios-51).

Aether H9 co-sim plan (when Next returns to H9): dual-bank PE context (ctx0/ctx1) store/load of `{root,size,parity,cbound,is_root}` + owned edge growth; TB proves 1-cycle switch restores state bit-identical; **no** claim of Stim-scale Helios-n until FPGA synth budget exists.

**M39 done:** plan executed — see `Docs/Helios_n_H9` + `rtl/aether_uf_pe_lutram_ctx.sv`.

